{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span class="text-evolution";">Evolved Wizard</span>}}
{{Evolved Card Infobox|Cost=5|CycleCost=1|Rarity=Rare|Type=Troop|Arena=Spell Valley|ReleaseDate=6 May 2024}}
{{Quote|Is it hot in here or is it just him? Wizard is now outfitted with a fancy fiery shield. Upon breaking, the shield explodes, dealing Damage and pushing nearby enemies back.}}

The Wizard's Evolution is a {{Rarity|Rare}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked with 6 Evolution Shards. It spawns a Wizard with identical stats to the original. Once deployed, a Fire Shield will appear around the Wizard, preventing him from dying in 1 attack. Once the shield is destroyed, all pushback capable [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] within 3 tiles of the Wizard will be pushed back by 3 tiles and take high damage. He takes the appearance of a man who has glowing pink eyes, brown eyebrows, and a goatee, and wears a violet cloak with brass-colored linings and boots, a team-colored shirt, pants and wristbands, and a golden belt chain with the [[Card Evolution]] symbol in the center. The Wizard's Evolution costs 5 [[Elixir]] and requires 1 cycle to deploy.

== Strategy ==
*The Evolved Wizard is a great defensive troop against [[Battle Decks|decks]] utilizing many swarm cards due to his large amount of splash damage.
**Additionally, unlike the regular [[Wizard]], the Evolved Wizard’s shield does enough damage to destroy [[Minions]] and [[Goblins]], allowing the user to place him directly in the center of a massive group of these troops to instantly wipe them out.
*The Evolved Wizard can be situationally ignored depending on the [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troop]] used by the opponent. If the [[Tower Princess]] is in use, the Evolved Wizard will do about half of the [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]] when left alone while the [[Cannoneer]] and [[Dagger Duchess]] will reduce this from slightly less than half to slight chip damage of the Crown Tower respectively.
*The Evolved Wizard has good synergy with the [[Giant]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Golem]]. The Evolved Wizard’s high damage will cripple or even destroy tank killers, such as [[Hunter]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Prince]], and [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], meant to defend the Giant/Lava Hound/Golem and his heavy splash damage will easily wipe out small and large swarms, such as [[Goblin Gang]], [[Skeleton Army]], Royal Recruits, [[Minion Horde]], [[Bats/Evolution|Evolved Bats]], and [[Barbarians]]. Also, the Giant will be taking hits for the Evolved Wizard, keeping him alive longer to take out more defensive troops.
*With the help of any tower troop and [[Goblins]] or [[Skeletons]], the Evolved Wizard can fully counter the [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Evolved Royal Recruits]] for a +1 Elixir trade. Additionally, the Evolved Wizard will survive, setting up for a potential counterattack.
*Like the regular Wizard, the Evolved Wizard has great synergy when paired with [[Tornado]] and [[Valkyrie/Evolution|Evolved Valkyrie]], The Tornado effect will pull opposing troops into the Wizard's splash radius, allowing him to hit more targets and deal more damage.
*Like the [[Dark Prince]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon Cart]], or [[Guards]], the Evolved Wizard cannot be destroyed in one hit by anything due to his shield, making cards like [[Rocket]], [[Lightning]], and [[Fireball]] almost entirely ineffective against him until the shield is destroyed. Although, small [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] like [[The Log]], [[Giant Snowball]], and [[Zap]] can destroy his shield. Therefore, small spells or a troop immune to pushback are ideal to safely destroy the shield and take out the Evolved Wizard.
*The Evolved Wizard is very effective against the [[Lava Hound]]. The Lava Hound itself can be quickly dispatched by his high damage while the Lava Pups are easily destroyed by his splash damage, causing minimal damage to be done to the Crown Tower in most cases.
*With the help of a Crown Tower, the [[Royal Delivery]] can fully counter the Evolved Wizard for a +2 Elixir trade. The delivery should ideally be deployed on top of the Evolved Wizard, where the [[Royal Recruits|Royal Recruit]] can distract and help take it out after being knocked back by the Fire Shield.
*If a [[Miner]] is placed on the inside corner of a Tower Princess, you can place the Evolved Wizard to get the Miner to knock himself into the [[King's Tower|King Tower]] from the Fire Shield’s explosion, potentially activating it if set up properly.
*With the help of a Crown Tower and placed in the center of the user’s side, the Evolved Wizard can fully counter the [[Elite Barbarians]] for a +1 positive Elixir trade. This makes him ideal at countering decks that utilize the Elite Barbarians inside of a larger group of troops, such as [[Elixir Golem]].
**Conversely, the Evolved Wizard has great synergy with the Elixir Golem as his shield and high damage ranged attacks severely discourage the opponent from placing most units next to the Elixir Golem to take it out; doing so would likely cause their defense to be destroyed by the Evolved Wizard. Instead, they’ll be forced to defend the Evolved Wizard first, giving ample time for the Elixir Golem to deal significant damage to the Crown Tower.
*The Evolved Wizard may be substituted for other [[Card Evolution|Card Evolutions]] with consistent splash damage, such as the [[Firecracker/Evolution|Evolved Firecracker]] and [[Bomber/Evolution|Evolved Bomber]], based on the user's deck choices and other preferences.
*If the user is up Elixir, a [[Mega Knight]] can easily prevent a small push that includes the Evolved Wizard. His spawn damage instantly destroys the shield and weakens all troops within the push, allowing for his regular attacks to finish it off.<center>

